# CODEOWNERS — defines path ownership for branch protection
#
# Platform support:
#   GitHub   — fully supported (free for public repos, Team+ for private)
#   Gitea    — supported since 1.21
#   GitLab   — requires Premium/Ultimate (CE users: see docs/git-permissions.md)
#
# Rules:
#   - Last matching pattern wins
#   - beacon owns everything by default
#   - Each clerk owns only their own hosts/clerks/<name>/ directory
#   - Changes outside a clerk's own directory require beacon's review
#
# Combined with branch protection on main:
#   - All pushes go through PRs
#   - Clerk PRs touching only their own directory → auto-merge (via CI)
#   - Clerk PRs touching shared paths → blocked until beacon approves

# Default: beacon owns everything
*                                   @beacon

# Shared modules and secrets — explicit beacon ownership (redundant but clear)
/modules/                           @beacon
/secrets/                           @beacon
/lib/                               @beacon
/.sops.yaml                         @beacon
/flake.nix                          @beacon
/flake.lock                         @beacon

# Clerk directories — each clerk owns their own
/hosts/clerks/default/              @openclaw-default
/hosts/clerks/technician/           @openclaw-technician

# Shared clerk config — beacon only (not individual clerks)
/hosts/clerks/common/               @beacon
/hosts/clerks/example/              @beacon
